# a-base-beside-a-robot-road — `plans/30` R8, and it is the CONTROL.
#
# ⚠⚠ **THE SAME MAP, THE SAME WALL, THE SAME WAVES AND THE SAME ROAD.**
# What moves is four numbers: the round runs at the FAR end of the road
# instead of at the base's own end, so no hex of it is inside the
# scrambler bubble and no hauler ever loses its link.
#
# ⚠ `a-road-that-passes-by`'s rule with a new mechanism: **the distance
# of the SOURCE is not the question; the ROUTE is.**

echo a base beside a robot road: the traffic never notices it

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 11 0
marker 11 0 spawn 3

count markers 2 2
do toggle_mode

# The base — `a-defended-base.keys`'s own patch, unchanged.
palette 5
drag -3 -2 12 -2
drag -3 -1 12 -1
drag -3 0 12 0
drag -3 1 12 1
drag -3 2 12 2

# ⚠ The ROAD, three rows along the base's southern flank and running far
# east.  It is painted identically in both halves of the pair — only the
# round's anchors move.
#
# ⚠⚠ **It starts EAST of the wall on purpose.**  A road that ran past the
# wall's end would let its traffic walk into the base without touching
# it, and the file would be measuring the gap rather than the traffic.
drag 6 3 74 3
drag 6 4 74 4
drag 6 5 74 5

# The wall, sealing the base from the road as well as from the spawn.
# ⚠ The road does not reach past it: rows 3-5 are painted only from
# q = 6, so the base's western half is sealed by the wall and by the sea
# alike.
palette 9
click 5 -2
click 5 -1
click 5 0
click 5 1
click 5 2
kind 5 0 wall

# ── The road's traffic ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ A depot and a face at the FAR end of the road — the round's nearest
# hex is 36 out, past the bubble's 25, so the base is never on this
# edge of the graph at all.
poi face 70 4
route 0 haul robot 4 36 4 0 0

# The player, at the core.  ⚠ The materialiser measures from the PLAYER;
# the bubble measures from the CORE.
park 0 0
player on 0 0 0

# ── The waves ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠⚠ **THREE, WHERE `a-defended-base.keys` SENDS FIVE AND THEN EIGHT,
# AND THE SIZE IS THE WHOLE MEASUREMENT.**  The siege front is the
# WALL'S WIDTH (`@M020`) — about four hexes on a five-row wall — so a
# wave of eight already saturates it and four more bodies change
# NOTHING.  Swept: the road is worth **196** ticks against a wave of
# two, **146** against three, **10** against five and **0** against
# eight (`@M085`).
#
# ⚠ That is `CLAUDE.md` § a gate whose reading is already saturated,
# priced rather than discovered: the first version of this pair ran the
# authored 5 + 8 and read **118 against 118** with four extra besiegers
# plainly on the map.
wave 3
count alive 3 3
wallet 200.0 200.0


fall 800
ticks 264 274
wallet 0.0 0.0

# ⚠ THREE alive — the wave and nothing else.  The haulers are 36 hexes
# out and the game never even built their round: one subtraction a tick
# per POI, and no body (`@X344`).
count alive 3 3

snap r8_a_base_beside_a_robot_road
